    goldenhour:
      " === TIME OF DAY: GOLDEN HOUR / MAGIC HOUR (the hour just before sunset) === Set the scene at the iconic golden hour just before sunset — sky bathed in vivid gold-orange-pink gradient, low-angle warm directional sunlight kissing every surface, glowing rim-light around the subject's hair and shoulders, long dramatic golden shadows, magical cinematic atmosphere. Subject side-lit or back-lit by warm low-angle golden sun creating a beautiful glowing halo on hair/skin, rich amber tones throughout the photo, classic magic-hour fashion-photography quality.",
    bluehour:
      " === TIME OF DAY: BLUE HOUR (30 minutes after sunset) === Set the scene at the blue hour shortly after sunset — sky in deep saturated cobalt-blue and indigo gradient, the last warm glow vanished from the horizon, ambient light is cool blue, city lights and lit windows starting to glow warmly against the blue sky, romantic cinematic twilight atmosphere. Subject lit by mix of cool blue ambient sky-light and warm artificial light sources (streetlamps, shop windows, neon signs), classic blue-hour film-still atmosphere.",
    night:
      " === TIME OF DAY: NIGHT (full darkness with city lights) === Set the scene at full night — black or very dark sky, the environment illuminated entirely by artificial light sources (streetlamps, neon signs, shop window glow, car headlights, moon), warm pools of light against deep shadow, atmospheric nocturnal mood with rich nightlife energy. Subject lit by warm orange streetlamps or colorful neon casting moody light-and-shadow patterns, deep cinematic city-at-night atmosphere.",
    latenight:
      " === TIME OF DAY: LATE NIGHT / MIDNIGHT (after midnight) === Set the scene in the dead of night past midnight — deserted quiet environment, only a few flickering streetlamps or distant neon left on, deep silence, dramatic isolated nocturnal atmosphere with moody pools of warm artificial light against vast darkness, lonely film-noir mood. Subject lit by single warm light source against deep black night, cinematic late-night solitude.",
    overcast:
